          "value": "SHA-256 in the Vyper toolchain, two roles: (1) vyper/utils.py:237-239 defines sha256sum, a source-content digest used for compiler caches/annotation IDs (compiler/input_bundle.py:35-36, compiler/phases.py:160, ast/parse.py:300, ast/nodes.py:651-652) — an integrity/cache tag, not adversarial; (2) vyper/builtins/functions.py:651-720 implements the sha256 language builtin: constant arguments fold host-side via hashlib.sha256 (:669), otherwise it compiles to EVM precompile 0x02 (SHA256_ADDRESS = 2)."
